  "notes": [
    "Recorded from the original renderer on the S001 route1 stack (Linux headless Chrome, isolated CODEX_HOME): fixture-backed pinnedThreads.set/list, localThreadCatalog pages honoring excludeThreadIds, and a mock app-server that marks pinned threads with the fixed Pinned section. With that stack the Pin click keeps every Recents row (the S001 drop came from a stub whose pinnedThreads.list and catalog page did not reflect the pin).",
    "Pin click: the row moves under a new `Pinned` header at once (optimistic, within 100 ms), no toast at any time (sampled up to 3.5 s). The renderer sends host pinnedThreads.set(pinned:true) and writes the persisted atom app-server-pinned-thread-order-v1; the Electron host turns pinnedThreads.set(true) into app-server thread/section/move {threadId, sectionId: <fixed Pinned section>, beforeThreadId: null} (threadSectionEngine.setThreadPinned -> setThreadSection, main bundle). The renderer's own thread/read and thread/list refetches that follow are reads and are not required of the port.",
    "Rest state: the row action group stays `opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100` for pinned rows too, so the Unpin icon is hidden at rest and fades in on hover like Pin and Archive (dom entries `unpin-rest`, `unpin-hover`). The row title keeps the full 264 px track at rest.",
    "Refused write (host pinnedThreads.set throws): the row stays in Pinned for about 350 ms, then returns to its Recents place; no toast (sampled to 3.8 s); the persisted atom is written back. See `refused`.",
    "`Chat pinned` / `Chat unpinned` (appUndo.chatPinned) are the toasts of the app-wide Undo that re-pins or unpins; the Pin click itself shows none. Cmd+Z in the recorder is inconclusive (native accelerators do not fire from real keys)."
  ],
